     Even with breath attacks, if you're invisible or displaced the
monster might misjudge your location and not realize that it's next
to you.  If the spot where it thinks you are happens to be lined up
with where you actually are, you can get hit by the ranged attack.
(Once it targets your location with a melee attack, you'll know that
it's found you at that location and won't use its breath attack
anymore--unless/until you move to a different spot.)

     The breath attack of most interest is probably from dragons,
and since they can see invisible this situation doesn't come up as
much as it might.  Particularly since cloaks of displacement tend to
be ditched in favor of others which have better magic cancellation/
negation/whatever by the time dragons are encountered.


